**Handlers that never run warn at startup,** and 5.0 refuses to start:
- a command or autocomplete handler Discord never sends, such as an unregistered subcommand path, a renamed builder or an option without autocomplete ([guide](/docs/4.1/migrating#a-command-handler-discord-never-sends-logs-a-warning));
- a second `@Autocomplete` for one option ([guide](/docs/4.1/migrating#a-second-autocomplete-for-one-option-logs-a-warning));
- a command, message, reaction or autocomplete handler on a class that isn't a controller ([guide](/docs/4.1/migrating#a-handler-on-a-class-that-isnt-a-controller-logs-a-warning)).

**Changes in 5.0, warned now:**
- a re-declared handler on another route still answers its inherited one; in 5.0 its own routes replace it ([guide](/docs/4.1/migrating#a-re-declared-handler-that-keeps-its-inherited-route-logs-a-warning));
- between equally specific overlapping component patterns, the first listed runs; in 5.0, the more spelled-out one does ([guide](/docs/4.1/migrating#overlapping-component-patterns-meocord-5-prefers-the-one-that-spells-out-more)).
